  "result": "I fixed the clamping bug in `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py`. I haven't run the tests or added a new one.\n\nFor an open bound, the method moved the value the wrong way: it returned `bound - dir` instead of `bound + dir`. A value below an open minimum of 0 was clamped to -1, which is outside the range. A value above an open maximum of 10 was clamped to 11, also outside it. With the fix they clamp to 1 and 9.\n\nClosed bounds were not affected.",
